  "result": "The gate returned **OK** for `NRS_484B_283_1d2`: all 10 witnesses gave their expected verdicts, and the nine exception rules are composed.\n\nI used 2 of the 6 gate runs. The first was a mistake: I ran it on the untouched skeleton, so it returned `UNUSED_CLAIM` because nothing was written yet. The second ran on the finished files and returned `OK`.\n\n**What the rule says** (`NRS_484B_283_1d2.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** a pedestrian, written as membership of the pedestrian aggregate `DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian`.\n- **When it applies:** a pedestrian signal head governs a roadway or lane, and the pedestrian last stepped onto it while the head flashed \"Don't Walk\" with a countdown, facing the head within the reading's 30° and 40 m limits. The head kept flashing with the countdown from then until the observation before it turned steady.\n- **The countdown's end:** the head shows steady here, and that crossing condition held at the previous observation. The language has no \"previous observation\" operator, but `rises (¬ …)` says exactly this, so I declared no narrowing.\n- **If the step onto the road came before the recording**, the rule reports unknown, as the record requires.\n- **The duty:** for every head and region selected that way, the pedestrian is no longer on the region. The obligation repeats the full selection so it refers to the same region.\n- **Exceptions:** seven are written as \"does not apply\" with the subject passed through. The two LVMC_11_46_030 limbs are written as \"no road user `v` in the scene engages either one\".\n\n**Witnesses** (`NRS_484B_283_1d2.lean` in `TrafficSpecWitness`): one street with a roadway, sidewalks on both sides, a marked crosswalk, and the head 18 m ahead of the pedestrian's entry point. Besides the five planned scenes, I added five branch tests:\n- `branch_1`: a lane-only street, so the lane case is tested.\n- `branch_2`: the pedestrian faces away from the head.\n- `branch_3`: the pedestrian's heading is 45° off the head.\n- `branch_4`: the head is 59 m away, beyond the 40 m limit.\n- `branch_5`: the head governs a different roadway.\n\nI declared no narrowings, and I found no defect in the node. The run log and choices are in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
